      "content": "GREAT GADDESDEN        GADDESDEN ROW TL 01 SE                                         (North side) 4/85                                    Sundial at Ragged Hall -                                       9m to N of house GV                                      II Sundial. 1716 dial on early C20 pedestal. Brass plate and gnomon on buff terra-cotta moulded pedestal. A square engraved dial plate about 200mm square with angular openwork gnomon. Square-section terra-cotta pillar about lm high with square top and base. Lotus leaf ornament to cap and each face of shaft. Inscription 'This Dial was made for/John St. Alban in 1716 for/Alfoxton Hall Alfoxton Devonshire/ Wordsworth and Coleridge/ are known to have been there/ in 1796'. Listing NGR: TL0611312052"
    }
